-- CC_0519_fremont_unified_trustee_areas.sql
-- CC_0519: Fremont Unified School District (Alameda County, CA) -- one address, one trustee.
--
-- PROBLEM. FUSD elects its 5 trustees BY TRUSTEE AREA (by-trustee-area since the 2020 elections under the CVRA;
-- the district's own page: "transitioned to a by-trustee area election system in the 2019-2020 school year").
-- All 5 board offices hung off ONE whole-district SCHOOL district (geo_id '0614400', G5420, district
-- 7a459708-1634-4d3b-b35a-ed4ca46de41a), so every FUSD address was shown all five trustees.
--
-- FIX (data only, the LA County trustee-area shape of CA_0219 / CA_0220):
--   1. 5 geofence rows, mtfcc 'X0002' (the school-subdistrict layer GEOFENCE_DISTRICT_JOIN admits for SCHOOL),
--      geo_id '0614400-ta-N', state '06' (FIPS, matching the G5420 row).
--   2. 5 SCHOOL districts, geo_id = district_id = '0614400-ta-N', state 'CA', mtfcc 'X0002' (the LA rows' shape).
--   3. Each 'Board Member (Area N)' office repointed from the whole-district row to '0614400-ta-N'.
--   The whole-district row and its G5420 polygon stay; with 0 offices it is not DEAD_GEOGRAPHY
--   (check-address-reachability requires offices > 0), exactly as ABC Unified '0601620' and Azusa '0603600'.
--
-- 🔴 OVERWRITTEN VALUES (the only UPDATE in this file). offices.district_id, all five rows, was
--   7a459708-1634-4d3b-b35a-ed4ca46de41a (geo_id '0614400'):
--     dbd6207f-b5d1-469e-82ce-5e7ce4a6264a  Board Member (Area 1)  Sharon Coco
--     5415b91d-a92e-484f-a086-c4bf77f6ae4a  Board Member (Area 2)  Larry Sweeney
--     7a095172-5e28-4101-9787-4022f0b33631  Board Member (Area 3)  Dianne Jones
--     4144cce9-5341-46d1-ae49-726ae27bfaf8  Board Member (Area 4)  Rinu Nair
--     95a508ab-74a3-41e3-ba84-8d4f4b8db58d  Board Member (Area 5)  Vivek Prasad
--   Undo: point those five offices back at 7a459708 (the new rows can then be deleted).
--
-- POLYGONS. Alameda County Registrar of Voters, "Unified School Districts" feature layer
--   (services5.arcgis.com/ROBnTHSNjoZ2Wm1P/arcgis/rest/services/Unified_School_Districts/FeatureServer/0,
--   owner AlamedaCounty.CA.US; "district and trustee area boundaries ... Boundaries represent voting districts"),
--   DIST_NAME 'FREMONT UNIFIED, AREA #1'..'#5' (DISTRICT_ID 803..807), data last edited 2026-10. Fetched
--   2026-11-27 with outSR=4326, coordinates rounded to 6 decimals; the file is
--   backend/data/fremont-unified-trustee-areas/fusd-trustee-areas.geojson. Inserted with ST_MakeValid, unsimplified.
-- VINTAGE. A coverage measure cannot tell a 2019 map from the 2021 one (root CLAUDE.md, Verification rules), so:
--   (a) the source is the registrar, which conducts FUSD's elections on these areas and edited the layer in 2026;
--   (b) the five shapes were drawn and compared by eye against Exhibit A of FUSD Resolution 019-2122 ("Trustee
--       Plan Map A", adopted 2021-12-08, sent to the ROV 2022-01-26 by Fagen Friedman & Fulfrost): same layout
--       (Area 1 northwest with its strip along the north edge, the diagonal Area 2, Area 3 northeast, Area 5 east,
--       Area 4 wrapping the south), including the patch Plan A moved from Area 4 into Area 5.
--   NOT done: a side-by-side with the 2019 map (its PDF is image strips that did not reassemble). (b) is a visual
--   match, not a named-place anchor.
-- COVERAGE (measured against prod, read-only, before writing):
--   areas km2: 1 = 33.035, 2 = 12.542, 3 = 30.802, 4 = 71.976, 5 = 58.349; all ST_IsValid; max pairwise overlap 0 m2.
--   union covers 0.90128 of the TIGER G5420 outline (228.28 km2). The 22.54 km2 not covered is one 22.10 km2 piece
--   in San Francisco Bay (point on surface -122.1163, 37.5111) plus 7 edge slivers of 0.020-0.052 km2 (~0.25 km2
--   in all) where the ROV and TIGER lines differ. ⚠ An address inside a sliver now matches no trustee area and so
--   sees no FUSD trustee (it still matches the whole-district row, which holds no office). Known, not fixed here:
--   the ROV line is the legal one for elections and the TIGER outline is a generalisation of it.
--   union outside the TIGER outline: 0.96 km2.
--
-- TRUSTEES (unchanged by this file; this is the check that each office goes to the right area):
--   FUSD's own roster (fremontunified.org/about/board/board-of-education-members/, "Last Updated: July 30, 2026"):
--   Coco Area 1, Sweeney Area 2, Jones Area 3, Nair Area 4, Prasad Area 5 -- the same as our office titles.
--   ⚠ Ballotpedia's 2026 FUSD entry has Jones in Area 2 and Sweeney in Area 3. That is Ballotpedia's error: its own
--   2022 section (Sweeney Area 2 uncontested; Jones Area 3 defeated Kavouniaris 5,994-2,341) and the district's
--   roster both agree with ours. Areas 2 and 3 were on the 2026-11-03 ballot list and were cancelled (no
--   challenger; both incumbents return without appearing on the ballot -- absent from the ROV certified results of
--   2026-11-25).
--
-- @incumbency-decision: no-effect -- writes no essentials.office_terms row; only offices.district_id moves.
--
-- AFTER APPLYING: this writes geofence_boundaries, so it bumps geofence_version (CC_0511) and every stored overlap
-- answer goes stale. Warm the store straight after, from backend/:
--   npx tsx -e "const {warmGeoOverlapPairs}=await import('./src/lib/geoOverlapWarm.ts'); console.log(await warmGeoOverlapPairs())"
-- Apply with: node scripts/apply-migration-file.mjs migrations/CC_0519_fremont_unified_trustee_areas.sql
--   (geometry-heavy; do not paste through MCP).
BEGIN;

-- ─── 0. Preconditions: the whole-district row holds exactly the five offices, held by the expected people ───
DO $$
DECLARE n int;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO n
    FROM essentials.offices o
    JOIN essentials.office_current_holder och ON och.office_id = o.id
    JOIN essentials.politicians p ON p.id = och.politician_id
    JOIN (VALUES
      ('dbd6207f-b5d1-469e-82ce-5e7ce4a6264a'::uuid, 'Board Member (Area 1)', 'Sharon Coco'),
      ('5415b91d-a92e-484f-a086-c4bf77f6ae4a'::uuid, 'Board Member (Area 2)', 'Larry Sweeney'),
      ('7a095172-5e28-4101-9787-4022f0b33631'::uuid, 'Board Member (Area 3)', 'Dianne Jones'),
      ('4144cce9-5341-46d1-ae49-726ae27bfaf8'::uuid, 'Board Member (Area 4)', 'Rinu Nair'),
      ('95a508ab-74a3-41e3-ba84-8d4f4b8db58d'::uuid, 'Board Member (Area 5)', 'Vivek Prasad')
    ) AS v(id, title, holder) ON v.id = o.id AND v.title = o.title AND v.holder = p.full_name
   WHERE o.district_id IN ('7a459708-1634-4d3b-b35a-ed4ca46de41a'::uuid)
      OR o.district_id IN (SELECT id FROM essentials.districts WHERE geo_id LIKE '0614400-ta-_');
  IF n <> 5 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'CC_0519 precondition: expected the 5 FUSD offices with their known holders, found %', n;
  END IF;
END $$;

-- ─── 1. Trustee-area polygons (X0002) ───
